	"_note": "Probe fixture. Tests the claim that a bulwark, a cap rail, a hatch coaming and a mast are expressible with TODAY's primitives and no new code. Uses only the two colours already in the palette, so it must not add a draw call. Bow is -Z, so plan z=0 is the bow; the 45 degree taper occupies z=0..5 on this hull, which is why the bulwark starts at z=5 and staircases at the shoulder instead of following the stem. DRESSED, 2026-08-10: the crude box mast (walls 10/11) is gone and the vessel now carries a rig built only from spar and wire \u2014 9 m tapered main mast with spreader, radome, masthead light and whips; a raked derrick boom with topping lift, fall and hook block; two pairs of trawl gallows drawn as inverted-L polylines with blocks and warps running back to a trawl winch; a short aft mast; exhaust pipe and cap; shrouds, forestay, triatic and backstay all at sag EXACTLY zero; a samson post at the stemhead for the forestay to be made fast to; sidelights on the wheelhouse corners with the white masthead light above them; three cylindrical fenders on lanyards over the port side; four mooring bitts. 52 items. COST, measured on RenderingServer's own counter over the four canonical views: draw calls UNCHANGED at 8, because every fitting is painted / steel / wood \u2014 the three material buckets this plan already had \u2014 and the baker keys buckets on material alone. Triangles 8903 -> 10847 (+22%%). Geometry is what a rig costs; draw calls are not. ROOM PURGE 2026-08-10: the room primitive was deleted and this fixture's deckhouse went with it. What remains is the bare hull rig — bulwark walls, deck plates, stairs and items. Fittings that stood on the deckhouse now stand in open air on purpose; the superstructure is rebuilt from the sloped-plate primitive in the next wave, not re-authored out of walls.",
